<title>USA: Consumers 67 MW Mich. nuke resumes power.</title>
<headline>Consumers 67 MW Mich. nuke resumes power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumers Power Co's 67 megawatt Big Rock Point nuclear power plant resumed power output over the weekend following a repair outage, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Monday.</p>
<p>The plant, located in Charlevoix, Mich., was shut Dec 13 after a piece of metal was discovered in the turbine.</p>
<p>The unit was operating at 18 percent of capacity and was increasing power as of early Monday, the NRC said in its daily plant status report.</p>
<p>Consumers Power is a subsidiary of CMS Energy Corp.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627))</p>
</text>
